---
// ┌───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
// │ ⚠️  THIS PAGE ASSERTS FACTS ABOUT PRODUCTION INFRASTRUCTURE.              │
// │                                                                           │
// │ Hosting provider, country, sub-processors, email delivery and backup      │
// │ retention are all stated here as legal representations. **A change to     │
// │ production is therefore also a change to this page and to /trust.**       │
// │                                                                           │
// │ This exact drift already happened once: prod moved from Hetzner (Germany) │
// │ to Pointer (Greece) on 2026-07-17 and both pages still named Hetzner six  │
// │ weeks later, because nothing connected the two. See landing#343.          │
// │                                                                           │
// │ Every claim below was re-derived from the running system on 2026-08-30 —  │
// │ not copied from the previous revision. How to re-derive each one:         │
// │   plans/growth/notes/LEGAL_PAGE_FACTS_2026-08-30.md                       │
// │                                                                           │
// │ `tests/legal-pages-facts.test.ts` enforces that this page and /trust      │
// │ agree with each other and that retired claims do not come back. It cannot │
// │ check reality — only consistency. Re-verify against the box when you edit.│
// └───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Datanika" description="Privacy Policy for Datanika data pipeline platform.">
  <Navbar />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-20">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-4xl font-bold gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mb-10 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: August 30, 2026</p>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-slate-300 leading-relaxed [&_h2]:text-xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-white [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:space-y-1 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-sm [&_th]:text-left [&_th]:py-2 [&_th]:pr-4 [&_th]:text-slate-400 [&_td]:py-2 [&_td]:pr-4">

      <section>
        <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
        <p>Individual Entrepreneur Evgenii Timofeev<br />Mikheil Tsinamdzgvrishvili st. 52, Tbilisi, Georgia<br />Identification number: 302355868<br />Email: <a href="mailto:info@datanika.io" class="text-violet-400 hover:underline">info@datanika.io</a></p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <p class="font-medium text-white mt-4 mb-2">Account information</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Name, email address (provided at registration or via OAuth)</li>
          <li>Organization name</li>
          <li>Authentication provider (Google, GitHub) and associated profile data</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="font-medium text-white mt-4 mb-2">Billing information</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Payment details are processed by Paddle.com (our Merchant of Record). We only store card brand and last four digits for display purposes.</li>
          <li>We do not store full card numbers, CVVs, or bank account details.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="font-medium text-white mt-4 mb-2">Usage data</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Pipeline run history, transformation logs, and configuration metadata</li>
          <li>Feature usage metrics (model runs, connections, schedules) for billing</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="font-medium text-white mt-4 mb-2">Technical data</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Web server access logs — IP address, user agent (which identifies browser and operating system), timestamp, and requested URL</li>
          <li>Your IP address is also used briefly to rate-limit password-reset requests. It is held in memory for that purpose and expires within two hours.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Legal basis</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Provide and maintain the Service</td><td>Contract performance</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Process payments and billing</td><td>Contract performance</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Send service notifications (outages, security alerts)</td><td>Legitimate interest</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Improve the Service and fix bugs</td><td>Legitimate interest</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Comply with legal obligations</td><td>Legal requirement</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. Data Sharing</h2>
        <p>We do not sell your personal data. We share data only with:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Pointer (pointer.gr)</strong> — application, database and worker hosting. Greece, EU.</li>
          <li><strong>Aweb</strong> — off-site database backups, and hosting for this website. Greece, EU.</li>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> — CDN, DDoS protection, DNS and TLS termination. United States, served from global points of presence.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend</strong> (Plus Five Five, Inc.) — transactional email delivery: password resets and team invitations. United States.</li>
          <li><strong>Paddle.com Market Ltd</strong> — payment processing, as Merchant of Record. United Kingdom.</li>
          <li><strong>Google / GitHub</strong> — only if you use OAuth sign-in (authentication data)</li>
          <li><strong>Law enforcement</strong> — only when required by law or valid legal process</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
          The same list, with each provider's purpose and data location, is on our
          <a href="/trust#subprocessors" class="text-violet-400 hover:underline">Trust &amp; Security page</a>,
          together with the date of the most recent change.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Data Storage and Security</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The application and its database run on a server in Greece, in the European Union, operated by the hosting provider Pointer (pointer.gr).</li>
          <li>All data in transit is encrypted via TLS. The credentials you enter for your own data sources (database passwords, API keys, service-account JSON) are encrypted at rest using Fernet symmetric encryption.</li>
          <li>Access to production systems is restricted to authorized personnel only.</li>
          <li>
            We take a database backup every night. Each backup is kept for 7 days on the
            application server and for 30 days off-site on a second server in Greece, operated
            by Aweb, so that losing one provider does not lose the data. The off-site copy
            contains the same account data as the live database, which is why Aweb is listed
            as a sub-processor.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Account data is retained while your account is active.</li>
          <li>
            After account deletion, personal data is removed within 30 days. The 30 days is
            the off-site backup retention window described in section 5 — a backup taken
            before the deletion request ages out within that period, which is what makes the
            promise deliverable rather than aspirational.
          </li>
          <li>
            Pipeline run history, run logs and configuration metadata are retained for as long
            as the organization exists. We do not currently run a time-based purge of run logs;
            they are removed when the organization is deleted.
          </li>
          <li>
            Web server access logs are rotated daily and kept for 14 days, then deleted.
          </li>
          <li>Billing records are retained for 7 years as required by tax law.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of your personal data</li>
          <li><strong>Rectification</strong> — correct inaccurate data</li>
          <li><strong>Deletion</strong> — request deletion of your account and data</li>
          <li><strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a machine-readable format</li>
          <li><strong>Objection</strong> — object to processing based on legitimate interest</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">To exercise any of these rights, email <a href="mailto:info@datanika.io" class="text-violet-400 hover:underline">info@datanika.io</a>. We will respond within 30 days.</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-400">
          There is no self-service delete button in the product yet — account and organization
          deletion is handled by us on request, by email. We are building the in-product route;
          until it ships, email is the way to exercise these rights and it is the route we support.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>8. Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          The Service sets two cookies, and only two. Both are short-lived
          (10 minutes), <code class="text-violet-400">HttpOnly</code>,
          <code class="text-violet-400">SameSite=Lax</code>, and exist to protect the sign-in
          redirect against cross-site request forgery: one for OAuth sign-in and one for
          SAML/OIDC single sign-on. Your session itself is held server-side, not in a cookie.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We do not use tracking cookies, analytics cookies, or third-party advertising
          cookies. Traffic on this marketing site is measured with a self-hosted Plausible
          instance, which is cookie-free and does not track individuals across sites.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>9. International Transfers</h2>
        <p>
          The application, its database and its off-site backups are all located in Greece, in
          the European Union. Your account data and your pipeline data are stored there.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Three of our sub-processors operate outside the EU, and the personal data each one
          receives is limited to what its function requires:
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-2">
          <li>
            <strong>Resend</strong> (United States) delivers transactional email. Password-reset
            and invitation messages carry the recipient's email address, so that address is
            transferred to the United States whenever we send you one.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (United States, with points of presence worldwide)
            terminates TLS and serves our traffic from the location nearest to you, and
            therefore processes your IP address and request metadata.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Paddle</strong> (United Kingdom) processes payments as Merchant of Record
            and holds the billing details you give it.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Transfers to the United Kingdom rely on the European Commission's adequacy decision
          for the UK. Transfers to the United States rely on the EU Standard Contractual
          Clauses incorporated into each provider's data processing agreement, and on those
          providers' certification under the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework. We are happy to
          point you at those agreements — email
          <a href="mailto:info@datanika.io" class="text-violet-400 hover:underline">info@datanika.io</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>10. Children</h2>
        <p>The Service is not intended for users under 18 years of age. We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of material changes via email or through the Service. The "Last updated" date at the top indicates the latest revision.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>For privacy-related questions or requests, contact us at <a href="mailto:info@datanika.io" class="text-violet-400 hover:underline">info@datanika.io</a>.</p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
